# T-2696 — Substrate-smoke canary (verb-3 "claim work" end-to-end composition)
# Source of truth: /opt/termlink/.context/cron/substrate-smoke-canary.crontab (git-tracked)
# Installed to:    /etc/cron.d/termlink-substrate-smoke-canary (USER field syntax — do NOT load into a user crontab)
#
# scripts/substrate-smoke.sh (T-2151) proves the substrate's canonical
# work-stealing composition (create → post → claim → claim-transfer →
# worker-loop → verify-clean + four arc-demo regression gates) — and nothing
# executed it on a schedule. The stuck-claims canary (T-2556) watches claim
# STATE; this canary proves the claim COMPOSITION still round-trips daily.
# Verdict translation (T-2557 pattern): smoke 0 → healthy, 1 → FIRE (broken
# stage named), 2 → tooling. THE LOAD-BEARING REMAP: the canary prechecks hub
# reachability itself and exits 2 (non-firing) when the hub is down — smoke
# alone exits 1 on a hub-down create stage, which would fire the canary on
# every blip (T-2694 F2/G3 trap). Empty log = healthy. /canaries auto-discovers
# this log.
#
# Operator action on firing: hub was reachable, so a stage genuinely broke.
# Reproduce: bash scripts/substrate-smoke.sh (names the stage), then inspect
# /claims --all and `termlink channel claims-summary --all --only-stuck`.
# Ad-hoc check: bash scripts/check-substrate-smoke-freshness.sh
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Daily at 07:37 UTC — offset from the :13 mirror, :17 unconfirmed-delivery,
# :27 stuck-claims, :33 session-control, :43 frozen-husk, :47 task-finalization.
37 7 * * * root cd /opt/termlink && bash scripts/check-substrate-smoke-freshness.sh --quiet >> .context/working/.substrate-smoke-canary.log 2>> .context/working/.substrate-smoke-canary.log.stderr
